--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Modifications
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This software is derived from the original work by Zacccck
(https://github.com/Zacccck/Claude-MCP-Read-Email-Attachments). The following
modifications are Copyright (c) 2026 Danny Ho and are released under the same
MIT License terms above:

- Read-only by default: removed unrestricted outbound mail and local file
  access; the server requests only User.Read and Mail.Read unless email
  composing is explicitly enabled.
- Security hardening: upgraded vulnerable dependencies (pdf-to-img/pdfjs-dist,
  sharp, adm-zip, zod, MCP SDK); disabled code evaluation in pdf.js for
  untrusted PDFs; zip/rar/7z bomb protection with per-entry and per-archive
  size budgets checked before decompression; stopped writing attachments to
  the system temp folder.
- Vietnamese OCR: scanned PDFs are OCR'd with Vietnamese + English by default
  (configurable via M365_OCR_LANGS); language data cached in the app data dir.
- Opt-in email composing: send_outlook_email and list_sendable_files tools
  behind Claude Desktop extension toggles (drafts only, or send immediately),
  recipient domain allowlist, attachments restricted to a chosen folder
  (symlink/junction-safe) or copied from existing emails, large attachments
  via Graph upload sessions, recipient/attachment/size limits, and MCP tool
  annotations (read-only / destructive hints).
- Refactor: split the single server.mjs into modules under src/ (config,
  auth, graph, parsers, mail) with one file per tool, grouped into auth/,
  read/ and send/.
